{"title": "Sectional Mock #139 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>Raman fixes the sale price of his goods at 16% above the cost price. He sells his goods at 12% less than the fixed price. Find the profit percentage correct to two places of decimal.</p>", "q_hi": "&#2352;&#2350;&#2344; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 16% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 12% &#2325;&#2350; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["1.07%", "2.08%", "0.08%", "3.01%"], "options_hi": ["1.07%", "2.08%", "0.08%", "3.01%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Assume the cost price is 100.</p><p>Marked price = 100  X  (1 + 0.16) = 116.</p><p>Selling price = 116  X  (1 &#8722; 0.12) = 116  X  0.88 = 102.08.</p><p>Profit = 102.08 &#8722; 100 = 2.08.</p><p>Profit percentage = (2.08/100)  X  100 = 2.08%.</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Assume the cost price is 100.</p><p>Marked price = 100  X  (1 + 0.16) = 116.</p><p>Selling price = 116  X  (1 &#8722; 0.12) = 116  X  0.88 = 102.08.</p><p>Profit = 102.08 &#8722; 100 = 2.08.</p><p>Profit percentage = (2.08/100)  X  100 = 2.08%.</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the product of all the prime numbers between 70 and 80.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>70 &#2324;&#2352; 80 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["518337", "409457", "560946", "576727"], "options_hi": ["518337", "409457", "560946", "576727"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Prime numbers are numbers that are only divisible by themselves or 1.</p><p>The prime numbers between 70 and 80 are 71, 73 and 79.</p><p>Therefore their product = 71*73*79</p><p>Product = 409457</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Prime numbers are numbers that are only divisible by themselves or 1.</p><p>The prime numbers between 70 and 80 are 71, 73 and 79.</p><p>Therefore their product = 71*73*79</p><p>Product = 409457</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A man's speed in still water is 4 km/h more than the speed of the current. If the man takes a total of 10 h to cover 45 km downstream and 35 km upstream, then the speed of the man in still water is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; 4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 45 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 35 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 10 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["20 km/h", "18 km/h", "15 km/h", "22 km/h"], "options_hi": ["20 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "18 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "15 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "22 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let current speed = c km/h, </p><p>Still water speed = c + 4 km/h</p><p>Downstream speed = (c + 4) + c = 2c + 4</p><p>Upstream speed = (c + 4) - c = 4 km/h</p><p>Time = 10 h</p><p>45/(2c + 4) + 35/4 = 10</p><p>45/(2c + 4) = 5/4</p><p>2c + 4 = 36</p><p>2c = 32</p><p>c = 16</p><p>Speed of the man in still water = 16 + 4 = 20 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let current speed = c km/h, </p><p>Still water speed = c + 4 km/h</p><p>Downstream speed = (c + 4) + c = 2c + 4</p><p>Upstream speed = (c + 4) - c = 4 km/h</p><p>Time = 10 h</p><p>45/(2c + 4) + 35/4 = 10</p><p>45/(2c + 4) = 5/4</p><p>2c + 4 = 36</p><p>2c = 32</p><p>c = 16</p><p>Speed of the man in still water = 16 + 4 = 20 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>A seven-digit number 2B37A74 is divisible by 9. What is the number of possible values of (A + B)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2366;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 2B37A74, 9 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; (A + B) &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1", "3", "2", "4"], "options_hi": ["1", "3", "2", "4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Number = 2B37A74</p><p>Sum of digits = 2 + B + 3 + 7 + A + 7 + 4 = 23 + A + B</p><p>So, possible values of A + B = 4, 13</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number = 2B37A74</p><p>Sum of digits = 2 + B + 3 + 7 + A + 7 + 4 = 23 + A + B</p><p>So, possible values of A + B = 4, 13</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>The first line graph shows the production of product A and B (in thousands) during the period 2004 to 2009 and the second line Graph shows the percentage sale of these products.</p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/7aec52cd393b4acf4949fd7070ccfcec.png\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/139a5517aced16468357db02fecc6f03.png\" /></p><p>In the given line graph, what is the total sale of Product B in the year 2004 and 2008 together?</p><p></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2366; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326;, 2004 &#2360;&#2375; 2009 &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2357;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2344; (&#2361;&#2332;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2311;&#2344; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/7aec52cd393b4acf4949fd7070ccfcec.png\"></p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/139a5517aced16468357db02fecc6f03.png\"></p><p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2319;&#2325;&#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; 2004 &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; 2008 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["12500", "14600", "11950", "11825"], "options_hi": ["12500", "14600", "11950", "11825"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "\"<p> Total sale of B in (2004 and 2008) </p><p>55 &#215; 8.5 + 65 &#215; 11 </p><p>467.5 + 715 </p><p>ATQ,</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000899.png\"/>\r &#215;1000 </p><p>= 11825</p><p></p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p> Total sale of B in (2004 and 2008) </p><p>55 &#215; 8.5 + 65 &#215; 11 </p><p>467.5 + 715 </p><p>ATQ,</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000899.png\"/>\r &#215;1000 </p><p>= 11825</p><p></p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>&#8710;ABC are &#8710;QPR are similar and AB = 12 cm, AC = 9 cm, PQ = 8 cm, and QR = 6 cm. Length of median BD is 10 cm, then find the length of corresponding median in &#8710;PQR.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#8710;ABC &#8710;QPR &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; AB = 12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, AC = 9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, PQ = 8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; QR = 6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8710;PQR &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["10/3 cm", "20/3 cm", "55/6 cm", "7.5 cm"], "options_hi": ["10/3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "20/3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "55/6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "7.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=288 height=154 id=\"Picture 76\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11857/image012.png\"></p><p>Since &#8710;ABC ~ &#8710;QPR:</p><p>AB: PQ = AC: QR = BD: PS</p><p>12: 8 = 10: PS</p><p>PS = 20/3 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=288 height=154 id=\"Picture 76\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11857/image012.png\"></p><p>Since &#8710;ABC ~ &#8710;QPR:</p><p>AB: PQ = AC: QR = BD: PS</p><p>12: 8 = 10: PS</p><p>PS = 20/3 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The below figure shows the estimated expenses of a family whose total estimated expenditure was &#8377;2,50,000. Study the figure and answer the question that follows</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 31\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27251/image021.png\"></p><p>It was found that the actual expenditure on electricity was 10% more than the estimated expenditure, and the actual expenditure on rent was 20% less than estimated. All other expenses were same as that of the estimates. What was the total actual expenditure?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2310;&#2306;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; 2,50,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2310;&#2306;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2306;</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 31\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27251/image021.png\"></p><p>&#2351;&#2361; &#2346;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; &#2348;&#2367;&#2332;&#2354;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 10% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2341;&#2366;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2319; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 20% &#2325;&#2350; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2368; &#2341;&#2375;&#2404; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?", "options_en": ["&#8377;2,52,500", "&#8377;2,40,750", "&#8377;2,43,750", "&#8377;2,48,750"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;2,52,500", "&#8377;2,40,750", "&#8377;2,43,750", "&#8377;2,48,750"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Estimated electricity expense = 11% of 250000=27500</p><p>Actual Electricity= 27500*110%=30250</p><p>Now, Actual rent expense = 80% of 45000=36000</p><p>Now rest of the expense = (20+16+17+18)%of 25000=177500</p><p>So total expenditure = 30250+36000+177500=243750</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Estimated electricity expense = 11% of 250000=27500</p><p>Actual Electricity= 27500*110%=30250</p><p>Now, Actual rent expense = 80% of 45000=36000</p><p>Now rest of the expense = (20+16+17+18)%of 25000=177500</p><p>So total expenditure = 30250+36000+177500=243750</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A takes 2 hours 30 minutes more than B to walk 40 km. If A doubles his speed, then he can make it in 1 hour less than B. How much time (in hours) does A require for walking a 40 km distance?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2325;&#2379; 40 km &#2325;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; B &#2360;&#2375; 2 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; 30 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; B &#2360;&#2375; 1 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2325;&#2379; 40 km &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["9", "7", "5", "6"], "options_hi": ["9", "7", "5", "6"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let speeds of A and B is 'a' and 'b' respectively.</p><p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=160 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image108.png\"></p><p><img width=80 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image109.png\"></p><p><img width=164 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image110.png\"></p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p><img width=116 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image111.png\"></p><p><img width=61 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image112.png\"></p><p>a = 40/7 km/h</p><p>Time taken by A to walk 40 km distance = 40 &div; (40/7)</p><p>= 7 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let speeds of A and B is 'a' and 'b' respectively.</p><p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=160 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image108.png\"></p><p><img width=80 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image109.png\"></p><p><img width=164 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image110.png\"></p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p><img width=116 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image111.png\"></p><p><img width=61 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24643/image112.png\"></p><p>a = 40/7 km/h</p><p>Time taken by A to walk 40 km distance = 40 &div; (40/7)</p><p>= 7 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the remainder of function 20a<sup>3</sup> -7a<sup>2</sup> + 4a + 7 when it is divided by 5a + 2? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2347;&#2364;&#2306;&#2325;&#2381;&#2358;&#2344; 20a<sup>3</sup> -7a<sup>2</sup> + 4a + 7 &#2325;&#2379; 5a + 2 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["7", "2", "3", "4"], "options_hi": ["7", "2", "3", "4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=226 height=141 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p26465/image008.png\" ></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=226 height=141 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p26465/image008.png\" ></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;Find the value of x if base area, volume and height of a prism are&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">9&radic;3", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354;, &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">9&radic;3", "options_en": ["3", "3&radic;3", "2&radic;3", "2"], "options_hi": ["3", "3&radic;3", "2&radic;3", "2"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "\"<p>Volume of prism = area of base &#215; height</p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/573e7463cee5dfb237b63b5c276626f4.png\"> </p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p>Volume of prism = area of base &#215; height</p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/573e7463cee5dfb237b63b5c276626f4.png\"> </p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Y and Z are two positive integers such that Y*Z = 75. Which of the following cannot be the value of Y  -  Z?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2328;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["10", "32", "74", "22"], "options_hi": ["1000000", "2160000", "194000", "12500000"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Y*Z = 75 = 1 * 3 * 5 * 5</p><p>Pairs of YZ = (1, 75), (3, 25), (5, 15)</p><p>Y  -  Z = 75  -  1 = 74</p><p>Or 25  -  3 = 22</p><p>Or 15  -  5 = 10 </p><p>Hence, option 'b' is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Y*Z = 75 = 1 * 3 * 5 * 5</p><p>Pairs of YZ = (1, 75), (3, 25), (5, 15)</p><p>Y  -  Z = 75  -  1 = 74</p><p>Or 25  -  3 = 22</p><p>Or 15  -  5 = 10 </p><p>Hence, option 'b' is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a 1250 m race, P runs at 25 km/h. P gives Q a head start of 50 m and still beats him by 12 seconds. Find the speed of Q. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>1250 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, P, 25 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; P, Q &#2360;&#2375; 50 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2352;&#2361;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2349;&#2368; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; Q &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["19.6 km/h", "22.4 km/h", "22.5 km/h", "18.4 km/h"], "options_hi": ["19.6 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "22.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "22.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "18.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><b>[To convert km/h in m/s, multiply with 5/18] </b></p><p>25 km/h = 125/18 m/s</p><p>Time taken by P to cover 1250 m = 1250/(125/18) = 180 seconds </p><p>Distance covered by Q = 1250  -  50 = 1200 m</p><p>Time taken by Q to cover 1200 m = 180 + 12 = 192 seconds </p><p>Hence, the speed of Q = 1200/ 192 = 6.25 m/s = 6.25 * 18/5 = 22.5 km/h </p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b>[To convert km/h in m/s, multiply with 5/18] </b></p><p>25 km/h = 125/18 m/s</p><p>Time taken by P to cover 1250 m = 1250/(125/18) = 180 seconds </p><p>Distance covered by Q = 1250  -  50 = 1200 m</p><p>Time taken by Q to cover 1200 m = 180 + 12 = 192 seconds </p><p>Hence, the speed of Q = 1200/ 192 = 6.25 m/s = 6.25 * 18/5 = 22.5 km/h </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>A dishonest shopkeeper sells Peas at Rs. 20/kg which he has bought at Rs. 12/kg and he is giving 800 gm instead of 1000 gm. find his profit percentage(rounded off to two decimal places).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2312;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; 20 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; 12 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2346;&#2352; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2361; 1000 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; 800 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2342;&#2375; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; (&#2342;&#2379; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;)&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["90.33%", "95.18%", "110.25%", "108.33%"], "options_hi": ["90.33%", "95.18%", "110.25%", "108.33%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Shopkeeper buys sugar at Rs. 12/kg</p><p>Sells at Rs. 20/kg</p><p>He gives 800 grams of peas but charges for 1000 grams.</p><p>Effective selling price per kg = 20/0.8 = Rs. 25/kg</p><p>Profit/kg = 25  -  12 = Rs. 13/kg</p><p>Required profit percentage = 13/12 * 100 = 108.33%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Shopkeeper buys sugar at Rs. 12/kg</p><p>Sells at Rs. 20/kg</p><p>He gives 800 grams of peas but charges for 1000 grams.</p><p>Effective selling price per kg = 20/0.8 = Rs. 25/kg</p><p>Profit/kg = 25  -  12 = Rs. 13/kg</p><p>Required profit percentage = 13/12 * 100 = 108.33%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The radii of two circle are 5 cm and 10 cm and the distance between their centres is 17 cm. Find the length of the transverse common tangent</p>", "q_hi": "&#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 17 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341; &#2313;&#2349;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["9 cm", "8 cm", "6 cm", "7.5 cm"], "options_hi": ["9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "7.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Here R<sub>1</sub>=5 cm</p><p>R<sub>2</sub>=17 cm</p><p>Distance=10 cm</p><p>Formula=L= &radic;(d<sup>2</sup>-(R<sub>1</sub>+R<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>Here (R<sub>1</sub>+R<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup>=15<sup>2</sup>=225</p><p>d<sup>2</sup>=17<sup>2</sup>=289</p><p>so L=&radic;(289-225)=8cm.</p><p>option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here R<sub>1</sub>=5 cm</p><p>R<sub>2</sub>=17 cm</p><p>Distance=10 cm</p><p>Formula=L= &radic;(d<sup>2</sup>-(R<sub>1</sub>+R<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>Here (R<sub>1</sub>+R<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup>=15<sup>2</sup>=225</p><p>d<sup>2</sup>=17<sup>2</sup>=289</p><p>so L=&radic;(289-225)=8cm.</p><p>option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the difference between the sum of prime numbers between 30 and 40 to the sum of prime number between 40 and 50?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; n &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["64", "65", "63", "61"], "options_hi": ["n(2n  -  1)", "n(n + 1)(n + 2)", "(n + 1)(2n  -  1)", "n<sup>3</sup>(n  -  1)"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Prime numbers between 40 to 90 = 41, 43, 47, 53, 59, 61, 67, 71, 73, 79, 83, 89</p><p>Numbers = 12</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Prime numbers between 40 to 90 = 41, 43, 47, 53, 59, 61, 67, 71, 73, 79, 83, 89</p><p>Numbers = 12</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two trains, 120m long and 150m long, travelling in opposite directions cross each other in 20 seconds. If speed of one of the trains is 4.5 m/s, calculate the speed of second train: </p>", "q_hi": "<p>120m &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 150m &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2354;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; 20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; 4.5 m/s &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2339;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;:</p>", "options_en": ["10.5 m/s", "12.5 m/s", "8 m/s", "9 m/s"], "options_hi": ["10.5 m/s", "12.5 m/s", "8 m/s", "9 m/s"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Effective speed = <img width=211 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20894/image027.png\"> </p><p>Effective speed = speed of first train + speed of second train </p><p>Speed of second train = 13.5  -  4.5 = 9 m/s</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Effective speed = <img width=211 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20894/image027.png\"> </p><p>Effective speed = speed of first train + speed of second train </p><p>Speed of second train = 13.5  -  4.5 = 9 m/s</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the area of the hexagon formed after cutting the corners of the sides of an equilateral triangle of side 9 cms</p>", "q_hi": "<p>9 cm &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2359;&#2335;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;-</p>", "options_en": ["2&radic;3/2", "29&radic;3/2", "27&radic;3/2", "20&radic;3/2"], "options_hi": ["2&radic;3/2", "29&radic;3/2", "27&radic;3/2", "20&radic;3/2"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=143 height=133 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p1084/image001.jpg\"></p><p>The diagram will be as shown in the figure.</p><p>Side of hexagon = 1/3 of side of &#916;</p><p>side of hexagon = 1*9/3 = 3cm</p><p>Area of hexagon = 6*&radic;3*a<sup>2</sup>/4</p><p>a= 3</p><p>Area = 6*&radic;3*3*3/4 = 27&radic;3/2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=143 height=133 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p1084/image001.jpg\"></p><p>The diagram will be as shown in the figure.</p><p>Side of hexagon = 1/3 of side of &#916;</p><p>side of hexagon = 1*9/3 = 3cm</p><p>Area of hexagon = 6*&radic;3*a<sup>2</sup>/4</p><p>a= 3</p><p>Area = 6*&radic;3*3*3/4 = 27&radic;3/2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two successive percentage decrease of 25% each is by what percentage less than two successive percentage increase of 25% each? (Round to two decimal places.)</p>", "q_hi": "25% &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368;, 25% &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;)", "options_en": ["50%", "43.75%", "22.22%", "56.25%"], "options_hi": ["50%", "43.75%", "22.22%", "56.25%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Assume original value = 100.</p><p>After two 25% decreases: 100 &rarr; 75 &rarr; 56.25</p><p>After two 25% increases: 100 &rarr; 125 &rarr; 156.25</p><p>Net change difference = 156.25  -  56.25 = 100</p><p>Relative difference = (12.5/56.25) X 100 &#8776; 22.22%</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Assume original value = 100.</p><p>After two 25% decreases: 100 &rarr; 75 &rarr; 56.25</p><p>After two 25% increases: 100 &rarr; 125 &rarr; 156.25</p><p>Net change difference = 156.25  -  56.25 = 100</p><p>Relative difference = (12.5/56.25) X 100 &#8776; 22.22%</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;What is the sum of the series&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["107/210", "11/21", "121/210", "11/210"], "options_hi": ["107/210", "11/21", "121/210", "11/210"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The series is (1/6 + 1/36 + 1/216 ...) + (1/7 + 1/49 + 1/343 + ..) + (1/8 + 1/64 + 1/512 + ..)</p><p> = (1/6)/(1 - 1/6) + (1/7) / (1-1/7) + (1/8)/(1-1/8)</p><p>= 1/5 + 1/6 + 1/7 = 107/210</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The series is (1/6 + 1/36 + 1/216 ...) + (1/7 + 1/49 + 1/343 + ..) + (1/8 + 1/64 + 1/512 + ..)</p><p> = (1/6)/(1 - 1/6) + (1/7) / (1-1/7) + (1/8)/(1-1/8)</p><p>= 1/5 + 1/6 + 1/7 = 107/210</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>The two parallel sides of a trapezium are 27 cm and 13 cm, respectively. If the height of the trapezium is 8 cm, then what is its area?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2306;&#2348; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 27 cm &#2324;&#2352; 13 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2306;&#2348; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 8 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["120 cm<sup>2</sup>", "160 cm<sup>2</sup>", "200 cm<sup>2</sup>", "400 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["120 cm<sup>2</sup>", "160 cm<sup>2</sup>", "200 cm<sup>2</sup>", "400 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Area of the trapezium = 1/2 * (sum of parallel sides) * height</p><p>=&gt; Area of the trapezium = 1/2 * (27 + 13) * 8 = 160 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Area of the trapezium = 1/2 * (sum of parallel sides) * height</p><p>=&gt; Area of the trapezium = 1/2 * (27 + 13) * 8 = 160 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Following pie  -  chart shows the monthly expenditure of Shiv on various items. If he spent total of Rs. 40,120. Find the saving amount of Shiv.</p><p><img width=305 height=216 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23668/image014.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2358;&#2367;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 40,120 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2367;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"305\" height=\"216\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23668/image014.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 27650", "Rs. 26590", "Rs. 27980", "Rs. 27880"], "options_hi": ["27650 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "26590 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "27980 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "27880 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Saving amount = 41% </p><p>Expenditure = 100  -  41 = 59%</p><p>According to question,</p><p>59% = 40,120</p><p>Savings= 40120/59 * 41 = Rs. 27880</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Saving amount = 41% </p><p>Expenditure = 100  -  41 = 59%</p><p>According to question,</p><p>59% = 40,120</p><p>Savings= 40120/59 * 41 = Rs. 27880</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A motorboat can travel a (M + 3) km in downstream in 6 hours and travelled same distance in upstream in 9 hours. If the speed of the motorboat in still water is 12.5 km/h, then what is the value of M?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2379;&#2335;&#2352;&#2348;&#2379;&#2335; 6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; (M + 3) km &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 9 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2379;&#2335;&#2352;&#2348;&#2379;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; 12.5 km/h &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; M &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["81", "87", "97", "85"], "options_hi": ["81", "87", "97", "85"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Downstream speed of the motorboat = (M + 3)/6 km/h</p><p>And upstream speed of the motorboat = (M + 3)/9 km/h</p><p>The speed of the motorboat in still water is 12 km/h,</p><p>=&gt; ((M + 3)/6 + (M + 3)/9)/2 = 12.5</p><p>=&gt; (M + 3)/6 + (M + 3)/9 = 25</p><p>=&gt; 5(M + 3) = 25 * 18</p><p>=&gt; M + 3 = 90</p><p>=&gt; M = 87</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Downstream speed of the motorboat = (M + 3)/6 km/h</p><p>And upstream speed of the motorboat = (M + 3)/9 km/h</p><p>The speed of the motorboat in still water is 12 km/h,</p><p>=&gt; ((M + 3)/6 + (M + 3)/9)/2 = 12.5</p><p>=&gt; (M + 3)/6 + (M + 3)/9 = 25</p><p>=&gt; 5(M + 3) = 25 * 18</p><p>=&gt; M + 3 = 90</p><p>=&gt; M = 87</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the circumference is equal to thrice of area of the circle. Find the diameter of the circle.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4/3 unit", "5/4 unit", "2/3 unit", "&frac34; unit"], "options_hi": ["4/3 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;", "5/4 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;", "2/3 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;", "&frac34; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>2&#960;r = 3&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>r = 2/3 </p><p>Diameter = 2*2/3 = 4/3 unit</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>2&#960;r = 3&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>r = 2/3 </p><p>Diameter = 2*2/3 = 4/3 unit</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following is a perfect cube?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>30 &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 40 &#2324;&#2352; 50 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1000000", "2160000", "194000", "12500000"], "options_hi": ["64", "65", "63", "61"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>For perfect cube, number of zeroes should be 3, 6, 9 etc.</p><p>(a) 1000000, since it has 6 zeroes, so cube root = 10<sup>3</sup></p><p>(b) 2160000 - 4 zeroes</p><p>(c) 194000 = 194 * 1000 =&gt; 194 is not a perfect cube)</p><p>(d) 12500000  -  5 zeroes</p><p>Hence, option 'a' is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>For perfect cube, number of zeroes should be 3, 6, 9 etc.</p><p>(a) 1000000, since it has 6 zeroes, so cube root = 10<sup>3</sup></p><p>(b) 2160000 - 4 zeroes</p><p>(c) 194000 = 194 * 1000 =&gt; 194 is not a perfect cube)</p><p>(d) 12500000  -  5 zeroes</p><p>Hence, option 'a' is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A fraction 3/5 is decreased by 2/5. The resulting fraction is then increased by 20%. What is the percentage decrease/increase in the value of the original fraction?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; 3/5 &#2325;&#2379; 2/5 &#2360;&#2375; &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; 20% &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;?", "options_en": ["Increase, 60%", "Decrease, 50%", "Increase, 50%", "Decrease, 60%"], "options_hi": ["&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367;, 60%", "&#2325;&#2350;&#2368;, 50%", "&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367;, 50%", "&#2325;&#2350;&#2368;, 60%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>&#8226; Original fraction = 3/5 = 0.6.</p><p>&#8226; Decrease by 2/5 = 0.4 =&gt; New fraction = 0.6  -  0.4 = 0.2.</p><p>&#8226; Increase this new fraction by 20% =&gt; 0.2  X  1.2 = 0.24.</p><p>&#8226; Compare final value (0.24) with original value (0.6).</p><p>&#8226; The drop is 0.6  -  0.24 = 0.36, which is 0.36/0.6 = 60% decrease.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&#8226; Original fraction = 3/5 = 0.6.</p><p>&#8226; Decrease by 2/5 = 0.4 =&gt; New fraction = 0.6  -  0.4 = 0.2.</p><p>&#8226; Increase this new fraction by 20% =&gt; 0.2  X  1.2 = 0.24.</p><p>&#8226; Compare final value (0.24) with original value (0.6).</p><p>&#8226; The drop is 0.6  -  0.24 = 0.36, which is 0.36/0.6 = 60% decrease.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}]}